Exception:-

(1) Recoverable: Exceptions can be handled using try-catch blocks, so the program can continue running.

(2) Cause: These usually occur due to mistakes in the program logic or input issues (e.g., dividing by zero, null pointer access).

(3) Types of Exception-
    - Compile Time (Checked Exception)
    - Run Time (Un-Checked Exception)

    Examples:
    -NullPointerException
    -ArithmeticException

 Error
(1) Unrecoverable: Errors cannot be handled by the program. They indicate serious problems that usually can’t be fixed at runtime.

(2) Cause: These are mostly caused by system-level issues like memory leaks or JVM crashes.

    Examples:
    -OutOfMemoryError
    -StackOverflowError
    -VirtualMachineError